1
00:00:05,568 --> 00:00:08,877
Got a drawing from CAD or a customer? Import drawing reads DXF, PDF and Illustrator files.

2
00:00:08,877 --> 00:00:15,982
This one is a spice-rack side, drawn in millimetres, with one layer for each kind of work.

3
00:00:15,982 --> 00:00:21,068
Shop layer names turn each layer into an operation: DRILL_12 drills 12 mm deep, POCKET_6 pockets 6 mm deep.

4
00:00:21,068 --> 00:00:25,356
INSIDE and OUTLINE are cut through. A layer with no rule, like NOTES, is listed so nothing gets missed.

5
00:00:25,356 --> 00:00:33,608
Pick the material, then Create part.

6
00:00:33,608 --> 00:00:39,796
The part arrives with its four operations, ready to check. Drilling runs first.

7
00:00:39,796 --> 00:00:43,151
Happy with them? Accept all.

8
00:00:43,151 --> 00:00:47,661
The Layers tab keeps every layer from the drawing.

9
00:00:47,661 --> 00:01:19,727
And the same Simulate check, here in 3D: dado, shelf-pin holes and handle cut-out.
